WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.240
A safe water infrastructure is a&nbsp;
necessity for a healthy community.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.120
It provides clean water to your taps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:15.920
it removes waste water and it protects the&nbsp;
community from flooding by managing stormwater.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.680
The government is currently reviewing how&nbsp;
these three water services are delivered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.920
across the country and along with other councils&nbsp;
we've committed to that first phase of reform.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.880
In return we've received eight million of&nbsp;
stimulus funding which is already helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.960
improve our water infrastructure.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.280
In the second stage of reform the government is&nbsp;
proposing that water services will be delivered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.880
by new regional or multi-regional entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.320
and billed to households separately&nbsp;
rather than by the Council.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.680
It's not clear yet whether signing up to&nbsp;
this stage of the reforms is actually going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.760
to benefit Waimakariri's ratepayers and&nbsp;
that's because our water infrastructure is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.000
well maintained, it's compliant and&nbsp;
high quality compared with other areas.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.000
Until we hear from the government later this year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.440
we won't know exactly how this will impact&nbsp;
on us but we will keep you up to date.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:25.840
Visit waimakariri.govt.nz/letstalk&nbsp;
to find out more.

